  "title": "Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in Image Optimization API when AVIF files are used",
  "summary": "A vulnerability in the underlying `libheif` library used by `sharp` which Next.js uses for image optimization can lead to remote code execution when AVIF files are optimized.\r\n\r\nUntil a fix has propagated, optimization of AVIF files is disabled.\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n- [GHSA-g89c-p67h-r497](https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-g89c-p67h-r497)",
